tive and mostly accurate. Vocabulary is appropriate to the task and varied. A variety of basic and some more complex structures is used effectively; occasional errors do not interfere with communication.\n  0: the work does not reach a standard described above.\nCriterion B: Message (0-6)\n  1-2: The task is partially fulfilled. Few ideas are relevant to the task; ideas are stated but not developed. Ideas are not clearly presented and do not follow a logical structure, making the message difficult to determine.\n  3-4: The task is generally fulfilled. Some ideas are relevant to the task; some are developed with detail and examples. Ideas are generally clearly presented and the response is generally structured logically, leading to a mostly successful delivery of the message.\n  5-6: The task is fulfilled. Ideas are relevant to the task and developed well with details and examples. Ideas are clearly presented and the response is structured logically, supporting the delivery of the message.\n  0: the work does not reach a standard described above.\nCriterion C: Conceptual understanding (0-3)\n  1: Conceptual understanding is limited. The choice of text type is generally inappropriate to the context, purpose or audience. The register and tone are inappropriate to the context, purpose and audience. The response incorporates limited recognizable conventions of the chosen text type.\n  2: Conceptual understanding is mostly demonstrated. The choice of text type is generally appropriate. The register and tone, while occasionally appropriate, fluctuate. The response incorporates some conventions of the chosen text type.\n  3: Conceptual understanding is fully demonstrated. The choice of text type is appropriate to the context, purpose and audience. The register and tone are appropriate. The response fully incorporates the conventions of the chosen text type.\n  0: the work does not reach a standard described above.\n## The examiners' rules\n- Within a band: all of its descriptors met gives the higher mark; most of them met gives the lower mark.\n- Completely off task: 0 for B and C (A can still be high).\n- The task misunderstood: B is at most 4.\n- No paragraphs: one mark off B, in any band.\n- Headers, dates, greetings, sign-offs and signatures do not count towards the 70 to 150 words. Under 70 words can still score well on A but rarely reaches the top band of B. Over 150 words is not penalised directly, but the examiner may stop reading, which can cost B.\n- Punctuation errors count. One error may be a slip; the same error repeated shows the structure is not mastered.\n- Vocabulary and structures copied from the prompt earn nothing.\n- Connectors and sequencing words are judged under B, not A.\n- Facts and opinions are not judged for being true.\n- The text type need not be named. A text type matching none of the three offered: C at most 1 (if tone and register fit). Named one type but wrote another: judged as what was written.\n- Writing to the wrong audience: C at most 2.\n- \"ustedes\" alone does not make a text formal.\n## Pieces the student's teacher marked (match this standard)\nHola amigo.\nMarks: A 4, B 5, C 2. good\n\nGive each criterion its mark with the descriptors met and missed, short quotes as evidence and the one or two changes that would move it up a band. List the language mistakes (wrong text exactly as written, the fix, a skill id, why). Set the flags honestly; the app applies the caps.\nSkill ids: accent.stress, accent.question, accent.diacritic, accent.verb, spelling, punctuation, agree.gender, agree.number, agree.verb, articles, ser-estar, por-para, tense.past, gustar, reflexive, verb.presente, verb.irregular, verb.perfecto, verb.indefinido, verb.imperfecto, verb.futuro, verb.condicional, verb.imperativo, verb.imperativo-neg, verb.subjuntivo, verb.infinitive, pronouns, possessives, comparisons, prepositions, connectors, word-choice, word-order, register","piece":"---\nprompt: p-1\nunit: G12.1\nwritten: 2026-11-09\nwords: 23\nmarks:\n  A: 0\n  B: 6\n  C: 2\n  total: 8\ntextType: blog\n---\n\n# Escribe un correo electrónico o un blog sobre tus vacaciones.\n\nQuerida Ana:\n\nAyer fui a la playa con mi familia y comimos paella en un restaurante muy bonito cerca del mar.\n\nHoy voy a estudiar.\n\nUn abrazo,\nMurtaza\n\n## Marks\n\n**8/15** · A Language 0/6 · B Message 6/6 · C Conceptual understanding 2/3\n\nok\n\n### A: Language (0/6)\n\n- Met: m\n- \"\"q\"\"\n- Next: n\n\n### B: Message (6/6)\n\n- Met: m\n- \"\"q\"\"\n- Next: n\n\n### C: Conceptual understanding (2/3)\n\n- Met: m\n- \"\"q\"\"\n- Next: n\n\n### Language mistakes\n\n- fui → fue (verb.indefinido): él\n","samples":[["---\nA: 4\nB: 5\nC: 2\ncomment: good\n---\n# x\nHola amigo.",{"A":4,"B":5,"C":2,"comment":"good","prompt":"","text":"Hola amigo."}],["---\nA: 4\n---\nHola",null],["---\nA: 4\nB: 5\nC: 2\n---\n",null]]}"##
